        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Increased detection and deterrence activity may dampen risk modestly, though effect is uncertain."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Frontline escalation risk and battlefield incentives for tactical use",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "High-intensity phases can incentivize chemical-weapons use as a force multiplier."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "Starting from a 0.25 anchor, integrate multiple convergent signals of chemical-agent use with stronger signals from credible intelligence and verified incidents. Apply Bayesian-style updates with directional weightings (up for verified incidents and credible intel; down for deterrence/monitoring; neutral for attribution). The combination yields a posterior around 0.75, with the range reflecting residual uncertainty about attribution and future battlefield dynamics."
  }
}

